<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92741" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥοχθ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dash with a roaring sound</i>, of the sea, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥόχθει γὰρ μέγα κῦμα ποτὶ ξερόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.402
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προτὶ δ᾽ αὐτὰς [πέτρας] κῦμα μέγα
					ῥοχθεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					12.60
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ κύματι πέτραι ῥόχθεον</span>
			<i>sounded with the dashing</i> of the waves, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.925
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥοχθεῦσιν δὲ κάλωες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					1.228
				</span></i>
			.—Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρεχθέω</span>.</div>
